A||N||2||Haze_Performance||radiator question ||||5||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||06-19-2000||05:16 AM||||Whats the proper way to flush a Fiero radiator?? (4 bangger) I would like to do a full system flush.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||06-19-2000||10:59 AM||||Haze, If you go to Trak Auto they have a flush kit that has a radiator cap with a hose fitting on it. This goes on the radiator. (for a 4cyl)remove the thermostat, then just remove the coolant hose that comes from the drivers side back by the engine. turn water on. when nothing but clean water comes out, block off the coolant line that goes to thr radiator and this will flush out the engine side. Turn off hose and let drain.<BR>Hook up the coolant line and raise back of car. Start filling with coolant at the tthermostat housing until front radiator starts to over flow, cap radiator, continue filling until it is filled, Install thermostat and start engine. let it warm up and make sure everything is working.<BR> <BR>||||reg||1
